      "identity_evidence": "Critic review for Skatesterre attributed by Metacritic to Shacknews.",
      "evidence_points": [
        "If you’re a longtime fan of the Tony Hawk’s Pro Skater series and desperately want a new game, and don’t care for what Activision is doing with it, you could certainly choose to play Skatesterre. You won’t have a good time, but it’s an option in front of you. The mechanics, controls, physics, and energy just aren’t there. And it isn’t really trying to do something different and whiffing; it’s the same blueprint, but stuff just doesn’t function properly. And there’s no personality to it besides “skateboarding game,” criminally underutilizing the athlete likeness in use. I walked in kind of intrigued to see what was on offer, and walked away shrugging. Them’s the breaks."
